  "worked_solution": "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n\u2016kx\u2016=|k|\\cdot \u2016x\u2016\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $\u2016x\u2016$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u20162x\u2016 & =1 \\\\ |2|\\cdot \u2016x\u2016 & =1 \\\\ \u2016x\u2016 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $\u2016-14x\u2016:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016-14x\u2016 & =14\\cdot \u2016x\u2016 \\\\  & =14\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
